---
description: |
  Deduplicates HarfangLab process start documents (`event.category`
  `process` with `event.type` `start` or `creation`) into one document per
  time window, host, executable, command line, and parent executable. Other
  documents, including process access documents, pass through unchanged.

  Each result stays an ECS process document. `event.start` and `event.end`
  hold the times of the first and last start, `event.duration` the time
  between them in nanoseconds, and `@timestamp` equals `event.start`. ECS has
  no field for the number of events that a document stands for, so
  `tenzir.count` holds the number of starts.

  The result describes the executable by its path, name, hashes, code
  signature, and PE header, the user, and the parent by its executable.
  Attributes that differ between starts don't appear: the process ID and
  entity ID, and the parent's process ID, entity ID, command line, and
  parent. The working directory appears only if all starts had the same one.
  The user and the executable's hashes are part of the grouping, so a start
  by another user or of another binary at the same path yields its own
  result.

  Windows follow processing time by default, so every document counts.
  HarfangLab delivers documents late and out of order, for example process
  starts from weeks ago when an agent reconnects. The window then only decides
  which documents share a result, and the times of the result still come from
  the documents. Set `event_time=true` to window by `@timestamp` instead, for
  example to replay stored documents. Event-time windows align to the Unix
  epoch and keep a separate clock per host, so one host with a skewed clock
  doesn't close the windows of the others, but they drop documents that arrive
  more than `tolerance` after their window ended, with a warning.

  A window closes once its host sends another document after the window
  end plus `tolerance`, after `window` without any document from the host,
  or when the input ends.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 1h
      description: Width of the deduplication windows.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 5min
      description: How long an event-time window waits for late documents.
    - name: event_time
      type: bool
      default: false
      description: Window by `@timestamp` instead of processing time.
---

if event.category?.first() == "process" and (
    "start" in event.type or "creation" in event.type) {
  // The outer grouping gives every host its own event-time clock and keeps
  // the host and agent records out of the per-window state.
  group {host: host, agent: agent, organization: organization?, ecs: ecs?} {
    window size=$window,
           on=(time(this["@timestamp"]) if $event_time else now()),
           tolerance=$tolerance, idle_timeout=$window {
      // Group by the attributes that the result shows instead of keeping
      // whole documents per group: the parent command lines are the largest
      // part of a process document.
      summarize event.kind, event.type,
        process.executable?, process.name?, process.command_line?,
        process.user?.id?, process.user?.name?,
        process.hash?, process.code_signature?, process.pe?,
        process.parent?.executable?,
        count=count(), start=min(time(this["@timestamp"])),
        end=max(time(this["@timestamp"])),
        _directories=distinct(process.working_directory?),
        _directory_count=count(process.working_directory?)
      directory = (_directories[0]
        if _directories.length() == 1 and _directory_count == count else null)
      this = {
        "@timestamp": start,
        agent: $group.agent,
        ecs: $group.ecs,
        event: {
          category: ["process"],
          kind: event.kind,
          type: event.type,
          start: start,
          end: end,
          duration: int((end - start) / 1ns),
        },
        host: $group.host,
        organization: $group.organization,
        process: {
          ...process,
          working_directory: directory,
        },
        tenzir: {count: count},
      }
      drop_null_fields
    }
  }
}
